# R8. The five open analyses

Each item names the `% TODO` it closes, the sample in the paper's own terms, the construction, the model, what to report, how to read it, and where the result lands. Samples, fixed effects, and inference are those already used for the neighbouring tables unless stated. Numbers quoted are from the current manuscript (Oct8.tex) and are the values to reproduce before any new fit.

Conventions: evaluation is Stockfish 18 at 100,000 nodes from the disconnected player's side; "competitive" is evaluation ≥ −100, "clearly worse" ≤ −300; the primary gradient model is the natural cubic spline of Appendix B.1 (boundaries −100/+600, knots 0, +100, +300, separate indicators for ≥ +600 and forced mates) with chooser, stage-band, speed, and month fixed effects, standard errors clustered by chooser, and the three planned contrasts f(100)−f(0), f(300)−f(100), f(500)−f(300) as one Holm family; the IV headline model is Table 5 Panel A (2,682,330 exposures; 4,324 cells of exposure month × exact time control × 100-point bin of the pair's mean rating; exposure-date and hour-of-week effects; the control set listed in Appendix D.2; shared-account-or-exposure-date CR0 covariance; Wald and Anderson–Rubin intervals).

