## 5. The author's accounts (TODO at A.1, line 579)

**Claim to verify.** "No reported rate or estimate elsewhere moves at the displayed precision when they are removed" (__PRIVATE_VALUE_1__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__; nine competitive-position opportunities and one grant; one exposure).

**Two acceptable resolutions.**

(a) Verify. Recompute without the two accounts: Table 1 (all counts and rates, including the competitive-minus-clearly-worse difference and ratio); Table B.1 row 1 (the three contrasts); Table 2 (the three correlations and the two second-year rates); Table 3 Panels A–C (rates and the joint model; also state whether either account is in the acquisition cohort at all); Table 4 row 1 (0.882); Table 5 Panel A. If every displayed value is unchanged, keep the sentence and cite this check in the replication notes. The arithmetic makes this the expected outcome: nine opportunities in 15,207,423 cannot move a rate at three decimals, and one account in 212,829 moves the Patron rate by at most 0.0005 points.

(b) Apply one rule. Drop both accounts at sample construction, add a row to Table A.1 ("Excluded: the author's accounts", with the opportunity count), rerun the pipeline, and delete the sentence and the three table notes that currently mention the exclusion.

(a) is an afternoon; (b) is a full rerun and removes the inconsistency rather than documenting it. Either is fine for submission; (b) is cleaner if the pipeline is being rerun for item 3 anyway.

